[{"id":"VRCE-2-58-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":1,"english":"Having unwittingly committed that great sin, I, with my senses oppressed through grief, thought within myself as to how I could mend it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7e63bdb04d72628564ce5466aec225ee7e47d461e16768707fcfe01f33aceb2c","compact":"8b06a73a526fe97f86e1275a96b596fd0711d713fed74090c244d9fae6986247","nasal":"eae5dd7ae433f626f833564c108fe6f82131ebe94228f553a6e2927def5d9e7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":2,"english":"Then taking up the pitcher filled with excellent water, I went by the way mentioned and (at last) reached the asylum.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.863,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bb3af7e6704ee032ff0f949e65b997ea299a0359c17ae650d3dc5ddf6895a136","compact":"73d4613ebbdc960ed67bf7ef2efddfd2a79b56bcc253be42e93bb83e665f61ed","nasal":"73d4613ebbdc960ed67bf7ef2efddfd2a79b56bcc253be42e93bb83e665f61ed"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":3,"english":"There I found his aged, infirm, forlorn, parents, without any one to help them in moving about, like to birds whose wings have been severed, keeping up a talk about (their son) without experiencing any fatigue, and like helpless ones feeding on a hope which had been blasted by me.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit