their preceptors, and individuals renouncing lives by fasting. He that is born in such a race cannot come by any evil case. Such a condition be his that has taken the life of you, my friend.'","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.448,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-38","DUTT-2-64-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058038","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa82325bf6abfe1568adf9ce5e3f0d533f0f8983cef81b2a05b8b6acb3d709e2","compact":"07bc2bb9dcb5c3997bb32144f03b73441d1e7dd65fc5060bdf699c06fb1a89e1","nasal":"07bc2bb9dcb5c3997bb32144f03b73441d1e7dd65fc5060bdf699c06fb1a89e1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-39","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":39,"english":"Having thus piteously wept, he along with his wife set about performing the watery rites on behalf of his son.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.768,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058039","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5025015e1dae5a965f1067b3009de36f23bf708c150d0da0bb35a106bcaeffd0","compact":"83d5e02534f48e48efa6d93ce0ead9faaa008abf705b1d91dfebe673a15201fc","nasal":"83d5e02534f48e48efa6d93ce0ead9faaa008abf705b1d91dfebe673a15201fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-40","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":40,"english":"Thereupon speedily assuming a celestial shape, the virtuous son of the ascetic by his own actions ascended heaven in company with Sakra. Then (returning) along with Sakra, the ascetic comforting his aged parents, addressed them, sa ing.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.431,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-41","DUTT-2-64-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058040","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"adce0ab36835a3