lishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"760078904801b9cbe053c382670dadd0b2f715bdc5afeacf2c628128efb0252b","compact":"b409a73f06e631c05b6d756242e208b4e3ae32dd07134a7ec7ca8332f601d2f7","nasal":"d8f080c274ea71c521aa23558397595c0285b0a0fa87ff563c07acef10356a0a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-44","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":44,"english":"Do you, O monarch, slay me on the instant. I do not grieve to die', you have by your shaft rendered me who had an only son, absolutely sonless.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058044","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"862813df440e4f9cc99fc2480d327b5b237737c6f85deec206a8730e54e39b95","compact":"d2742d6d243d865d1d75c0e3aae931c37c9d1a92798e5fd618f2e7c743406cdb","nasal":"d2742d6d243d865d1d75c0e3aae931c37c9d1a92798e5fd618f2e7c743406cdb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-45","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":45,"english":"Since this sorrow arising from the calamity that has befallen my son, is at present mine (through your instrumentality), I curse you. You shall even in this way find your death from grief born of separation from your son.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.19,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058045","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0f4e4d91bc000625441078281b70fdb5bb5adb78a071707ccafd269b63ed2fba","compact":"ab19e21f68d4ea4efb9bac66db31c7606d1a56ccfa201a4863b57a44721a1e9f","nasal":"18adca74d98d82d013e99d9e37232fd758c306f379112f908d90eb0d44ffc21d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-46","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":46,"english":"Since this sorrow arising from the calamity that has befallen my son, is at present mine (through your instrumentality), I curse you. You shall even in this way find your death from grief born of separation from your son.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058046","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"884d3dad8306b01adeea8c33768fc24bd82df284e9ca5ad0383cfe92fd4f01e3","compact":"a12d6c1f53c9cb2152616d004e15cc2f8b97295c23d4dbcd5f1cc15da1eb4616","nasal":"1cc46ff3a0c156379d14ec6fcf9f2da870e9cdd58bad32e16cbc0acdb13165d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-47","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":47,"english":"O exalted lady, even as a disease generated by one's taking rice with unhealthy curry, this danger is imminent in consequence of that act. O gentle one, the words of that noble-minded person are about to be verified in me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.433,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-51"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058047","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54e877d9a2e73e95a7c8b2dbd981391531b5977a81492ca061881320e3f67352","compact":"a88049f269f4bdfc3e7e097998e2ea14eeb53137cf2de7ec77acaff9b82c5408","nasal":"a88049f269f4bdfc3e7e097998e2ea14eeb53137cf2de7ec77acaff9b82c5408"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-48","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":48,"english":"People going to the mansion of Yama no more behold (their friends): If Rama touch me directly or otherwise, obtain the exchequer, and be installed as the heir-apparent, Meseems, I may yet live. O noble lady, what I have done to Rāghava in not surely like myself; but what (on the other hand) he has done by me is worthy of him.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.414,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-53","DUTT-2-64-54"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058048","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"729a3111d147dc939bd9eb92082baec01a4ac50c2cf4c2458139941a608238a9","compact":"a580ab78622cb698d34cdf29b8ca9b4c122cd51a7139d3a159dc246e57345ddb","nasal":"a580ab78622cb698d34cdf29b8ca9b4c122cd51a7139d3a159dc246e57345ddb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-49","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":49,"english":"But I do not see you with my eyes, and my memory fails. These envoys of Vivasvata's son, OKausalya, urge speed upon me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-56"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058049","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9184f92955d2eac401b5d1ad7e6c2131c33e7ec91768d299e364b214ca4f472f","compact":"abc108cd470129edf591f324df10875d9649c642577ae120377437ed0e8fc6f1","nasal":"cf1944fcd62a3103cc4345d51875c8b13a7f851b01d25570df99a481a9a40741"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-50","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":50,"english":"What can be an object of greater regret than that I during my last moments cannot behold the righteous Rāma having truth for prowess?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.931,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-57"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058050","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf12a07b3fcad461b67350edb2eade4a1fcbd8252bd6b7fecbd5fd9e72e84e9a","compact":"22b0da2a907e0deecdb152c8b35176adeb50c776abc53eca0c17f6e11281f67a","nasal":"22b0da2a907e0deecdb152c8b35176adeb50c776abc53eca0c17f6e11281f67a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-51","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":51,"english":"Those are not men, those are gods who in the fifteenth year shall again behold Rāma's countenance graced with elegant and burnished ear-rings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-59"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058051","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"49cd9bcb67054ceeaedb50840b71d1fa459e561ebc62a215c57312462cfcd901","compact":"b9213afcec4df7be56dac917b8386f4301e2b705f2b79839921fb46617ca733d","nasal":"888d1c1f0b834f897f62a21cfec06c91816af164067dec5704814661a7e50d2e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-52","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":52,"english":"O you of graceful eye-brows, blessed are they who shall behold Rāma's countenance furnished with eyes resembling lotus-petals, with excellent teeth and a shapely nose, like to the lord of the stars himself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.767,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-60"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058052","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"69f6ba941f0cde498ad7198908049bf1ca56be270111ffc07516034a1098cf23","compact":"49906e8f80587b71b750cfa685e71293f7db75c1f13dd340410e249baf56957e","nasal":"eb4dd596afbf3be017ecadea100057eb249646094d783be7b1308c14f61e69ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-58-53","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":58,"verse":53,"english":"Blessed are they that shall behold that fragrant face of his like to the autumnal moon, or the fullblown lotus. Thrice-blessed they who with delighted hearts, shall behold Rāma returned from the forest and come back to Ayodhyā, like to Sukra crowning the zenith?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.803,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-64-61"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2058053","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c1541472c25b8b2d5842e6d715555f77c328e220b0ba6274348e00c1145d13e","compact":"663d51b17ed236bfc29bbbc97aa26b0f46668011c2e8af0b9aa71e10ea3b1ecf","nasal":"c36f62fd14319018395783762c6